# Tablet-first layout for 2easy-mobile

- Assume the app runs on phones **and tablets** (iPad / Android large screens). `TARGETED_DEVICE_FAMILY` is `1,2`.
- Use `useLayout()` from `src/shared/lib/layout.ts` for breakpoints instead of hardcoding widths.
- Keep content readable on wide screens: center columns, `maxWidth` for forms (~460 phone / ~560 tablet) and page content (~840 tablet).
- Increase spacing, tap targets, and type size on tablet where it helps; do not stretch single-column forms edge-to-edge.
- Support landscape on tablets; avoid layouts that break when width > height.
- Auth autofill must keep `textContentType` / `autoComplete` / `importantForAutofill` so credentials from `2easyeng.com` can fill login fields.

# Launch & guest access (like the site)

- Main screen is always **Lesson plans** (even without login).
- Do not hard-gate the whole app behind auth. Login/registration are modal/optional.
- Features available on the website without login/subscription should remain available in the app (browse public catalog, search, level filters; open lesson prompts auth).
